    "body": "Thanks for updating the proposal above. Can you please also write some pseudo code of what you expect the actual user-facing workflow to look like?\r\n\r\nThat said, I am not sold on `DoubleFactorizedHamiltonian` class. With the work done in #1033 we will be able to instead store the low-rank 2-body integrals instead of the standard 4D matrix directly inside the existing framework. See for example how I implemented AO-symmetry aware 2-body tensors [here](https://github.com/mrossinek/qiskit-nature/blob/e7fa3cf998b0da64dc0ba4a9c9605edf44fb17a1/qiskit_nature/second_q/operators/symmetric_two_body.py).",
